          "noteText": "<h3>Diagnosis</h3><p>Multiple deep gastric ulcers with <strong>perforation</strong> and peritonitis. Nematodes in the stomach, moderate numbers.</p><h3>History</h3><p>Six weeks of weight loss and reduced appetite; treated for suspected gastritis.</p><h3>Weights and Measurements</h3><p>49.0 kg. Blubber 1.8 cm at the sternum.</p><h3>Digestive System, Mouth, Esophagus, Stomach, Intestines, Rectum</h3><p>4 cm perforation of the fundic stomach with fibrin on the serosa; about 200 anisakid nematodes attached to the gastric mucosa.</p>",
